---
source: crates/dreamd-cli/tests/cli_help.rs
expression: "subcommand_help(\"forget\")"
---
Remove one episodic event, the lesson state built from it, and the copies dreamd keeps of it.

Clears the live log, LESSONS.md, the recurrence counts, the decay archive, the migrate backup, every autosnap and memory branch (each is rewritten without the event; refs keep their names), and the search index (pruned, then merged so the text leaves the segment files). Prints a `cleared:` line, and one `remaining:` line per place a copy is still kept.

It never rewrites git history. When committed `.agent/` files hold the event, it prints how many commits, the first and last, and a `git filter-repo` command you can run. Until you run it, and until every clone and remote rewrites too, those commits keep the text.

Stop a live `dreamd watch` first; the command refuses while the daemon is running.

Usage: forget [OPTIONS] <EVENT_ID>

Arguments:
  <EVENT_ID>
          The event id to remove (`evt_` + 26 Crockford base32 characters)

Options:
      --dry-run
          Print what would be removed, and the memory files, branch objects and refs that would change, without writing anything

      --proof <PATH>
          Write a forget-receipt/1.1 JSON file to PATH after a removal: the event id, lesson effect, ledger root and orphan edges, plus `cleared` and `remaining` (where copies are still kept, git history included). It holds no memory content. Unsigned; not a proof

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
